From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:33:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: tests: stations and interfaces mac80211
 can find

Paths where the driver asks mac80211 for a station or walks its
interfaces had no test: main-test.c's stations and interfaces were the
driver's part only. It now has interfaces mac80211 lists and runs, and
stations that are mac80211's own (sta_info_alloc(), in its station hash
and list as sta_info_insert() leaves them).

- mt7915_main_test_drop_other_sta_real: a client authorized on one band
  is disconnected in the firmware on the interface it left; one whose
  wcid is already unpublished is left alone.
- mt7915_main_test_et_stats_sta: a station's counters in ethtool -S.
- mt7915_main_test_offchannel_nullfunc: a station interface's QoS null
  to its AP going off channel (PM set) and back (mt7996's path: mt7915
  has no channel contexts of its own; the test gives the interface one).
- mt7915_main_test_wed_txs: with WED, per-PPDU tx status counted and the
  BA session's timer refreshed.
- mt7915_main_test_inband_discov: FILS discovery and unsolicited probe
  responses to the firmware; none without a template or interval, one
  too large refused.
- mt7915_main_test_bss_info_sta: a station interface's BSS names its
  AP's wcid, found by BSSID.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/tests/main-test.c | 422 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 419 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

